  "reading": "On every shaped link only the final interval line is late (0.206 s with a 100 ms round trip and no queue; 0.62-0.75 s behind the 10 Mbit/s queue, with and without a second flow), while every other line's estimate sits within 2.5 ms of the earliest. Unshaped, nothing is late beyond 23 ms (the flow there runs at 27-58 Gbit/s and is CPU-bound). iperf 3.21 prints the last interval only after the end-of-test exchange with the server (iperf_client_end -> reporter_callback), which crosses the shaped link."
